[27.138434, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[27.198234, "o", "the model's answer (plain text):\r\n   Summary of your latest ticket: Hi, please reset my password. <img src=x onerror=\"alert('Model output just ran as code in your browser')\">\r\n\r\nthe HTML the vulnerable app puts in the page:\r\n   <p class='answer'>Summary of your latest ticket: Hi, please reset my password. <img src=x onerror=\"alert('Model output just ran as code in your browser')\"></p>\r\n\r\n"]
[27.19831, "o", "how a browser reads it (explained by Python's html.parser; no browser runs here):\r\n   element <p>: a paragraph\r\n   text: 'Summary of your latest ticket: Hi, please reset my password.'\r\n   element <img>: fetches 'x' straight away, no click needed\r\n      attribute onerror: runs \"alert('Model output just ran as code in your browser')\" as JavaScript if loading fails\r\n"]
